# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for G-TSAN (.port/tools/gates/sanitizers.sh
# --gate tsan; run_crate passes it through TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...:
# print_suppressions=1, so every match is listed in the crate log).
#
# Same rules as lsan.supp: every entry is a THIRD-PARTY race (a system
# framework or vendored C/C++), each with a row in
# .port/phase-2/SANITIZER_SUPPRESSIONS.md (ThreadSanitizer section, T ids)
# giving the reason and evidence, and a WHY comment directly above it (D6 rule
# c). A race in Rustty code is never suppressed: it is a finding (an N id, and
# a UD when Ghostty has it too), fixed with a regression test.
#
# No entry: G-TSAN's first runs (P7-W17, macOS; P7-W24, Linux) needed none.
# The first Linux run's rustty-xev reports (TSan's fd model, NEW-FINDINGS
# N514) are handled by running that crate's tests one at a time
# (TSAN_SERIAL in sanitizers.sh), not by a suppression.
